\bibitem{endgame-solving-exception}
End-game solving~\cite{Ganzfried15:Endgame,cprg:cfrd,Moravcik16:Subgames} is
  one exception to computation occurring prior to play. When the game nears the
  end, a new computation is invoked over the remainder of the game. Thus, the
  program need not store this part of the strategy or can use a finer-grained
  abstraction aimed to improve the solution quality. We discuss this as
  re-solving when we introduce DeepStack's technique of continual re-solving.

